Some themes


A model takes inputs and generates predictions;
A model is statistical if it delivers uncertainty quantification for the predictions and conclusions;
Model outputs are just like any other summary. It’s just our best guess;
All models are wrong, but some are useful;
Beware the reflex to interpret the model as “input causes output.” Maybe. Maybe not.

But in math terms…
\[
\begin{aligned}
y &= mx + b \\
\text{Output}&=\text{Slope}\times \text{Input} + \text{Intercept}
\end{aligned}
\]

